{"test_id": "B05-001", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "What are the minimum password requirements according to CCoP 2.0?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Minimum 8 characters", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.2.2"}, {"fact": "Must contain uppercase, lowercase, numbers, special characters", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.2.2"}, {"fact": "No common words or patterns", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.2.2"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 5.2.2, password complexity requirements requirements are as follows:\n\nMinimum 8 characters (critical) Must contain uppercase, lowercase, numbers, special characters (critical) No common words or patterns (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for identity & access management. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 5.2.2", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 5.2.2 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for password complexity requirements", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that password complexity requirements requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.2.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "positive", "related_section