{"test_id": "B05-003", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "What is the required timeframe for reporting cybersecurity incidents to CSA?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Critical incidents within 2 hours", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 7.3.1"}, {"fact": "Significant incidents within 24 hours", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 7.3.1"}, {"fact": "Other incidents within 72 hours", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 7.3.1"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 7.3.1, security incident reporting timeline requirements are as follows:\n\nCritical incidents within 2 hours (critical) Significant incidents within 24 hours (critical) Other incidents within 72 hours (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for incident management. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 7.3.1", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 7.3.1 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for security incident reporting timeline", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that security incident reporting timeline requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "7", "clause_reference": ["7.3.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "positive", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B05-004", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "How long must security logs be retained according to CCoP 2.0?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Minimum 12 months retention", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.3.2"}, {"fact": "Additional 6 months in accessible format", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.3.2"}, {"fact": "Audit logs must be tamper-proof", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.3.2"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 6.3.2, data retention requirements requirements are as follows:\n\nMinimum 12 months retention (critical) Additional 6 months in accessible format (important) Audit logs must be tamper-proof (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for logging & monitoring. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 6.3.2", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 6.3.2 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for data retention requirements", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that data retention requirements requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.3.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "positive", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B05-005", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "What are the network segmentation requirements for CII environments?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Separate critical systems from non-critical", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.4.1"}, {"fact": "DMZ for internet-facing systems", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.4.1"}, {"fact": "VLANs or physical segmentation", "tier": "supporting", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.4.1"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 5.4.1, network segmentation requirements requirements are as follows:\n\nSeparate critical systems from non-critical (critical) DMZ for internet-facing systems (critical) VLANs or physical segmentation (supporting).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for network security. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 5.4.1", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 5.4.1 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for network segmentation requirements", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that network segmentation requirements requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.4.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "positive", "related_sections": [], "test_