{"test_id": "B05-006", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "How often must vulnerability scans be conducted for CII systems?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "External scans quarterly at minimum", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.2.1"}, {"fact": "Internal scans semi-annually at minimum", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.2.1"}, {"fact": "After significant system changes", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.2.1"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 6.2.1, vulnerability scanning frequency requirements are as follows:\n\nExternal scans quarterly at minimum (critical) Internal scans semi-annually at minimum (important) After significant system changes (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for vulnerability management. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 6.2.1", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 6.2.1 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for vulnerability scanning frequency", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that vulnerability scanning frequency requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "positive", "related_sections": [], "