{"test_id": "B05-008", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "What are the backup requirements for CII critical systems?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Daily backups for critical data", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.6.1"}, {"fact": "Offsite storage required", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.6.1"}, {"fact": "Test restoration quarterly", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.6.1"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 5.6.1, backup requirements requirements are as follows:\n\nDaily backups for critical data (critical) Offsite storage required (critical) Test restoration quarterly (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for data protection. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 5.6.1", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 5.6.1 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for backup requirements", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that backup requirements requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.6.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "positive", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B05-009", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "When must encryption be used according to CCoP 2.0?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Data in transit encryption mandatory", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.5.1"}, {"fact": "Data at rest encryption for sensitive data", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.5.1"}, {"fact": "Minimum AES-256 or equivalent", "tier": "supporting", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.5.1"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 5.5.1, encryption requirements requirements are as follows:\n\nData in transit encryption mandatory (critical) Data at rest encryption for sensitive data (critical) Minimum AES-256 or equivalent (supporting).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for data protection. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 5.5.1", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 5.5.1 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for encryption requirements", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that encryption requirements requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.5.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "positive", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2