{"test_id": "B05-010", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "How often must cybersecurity awareness training be conducted?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "All staff annually at minimum", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 8.2.1"}, {"fact": "New hires within 1 month", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 8.2.1"}, {"fact": "Additional training for privileged users", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 8.2.1"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 8.2.1, security training frequency requirements are as follows:\n\nAll staff annually at minimum (critical) New hires within 1 month (critical) Additional training for privileged users (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for security awareness. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 8.2.1", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 8.2.1 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for security training frequency", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that security training frequency requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "8", "clause_reference": ["8.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "positive", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B05-011", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "When a CII function is outsourced to a third-party provider, who is responsible for implementing CCoP controls?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "CII operator retains ultimate responsibility", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 9.1.2"}, {"fact": "Must verify provider controls contractually", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 9.1.2"}, {"fact": "Regular audit rights required", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 9.1.2"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 9.1.2, third-party service provider control allocation requirements are as follows:\n\nCII operator retains ultimate responsibility (critical) Must verify provider controls contractually (critical) Regular audit rights required (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for third-party risk. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 9.1.2", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 9.1.2 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for third-party service provider control allocation", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that third-party service provider control allocation requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "9", "clause_reference": 