{"test_id": "B05-013", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "Can legacy systems be exempted from CCoP 2.0 control requirements?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "No blanket exemptions for legacy", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 4.3"}, {"fact": "Compensating controls required if not compliant", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 4.3"}, {"fact": "Must document risk and mitigation plan", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 4.3"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 1.6 (Waiver), legacy system exemptions requirements are as follows:\n\nNo blanket exemptions for legacy (critical) Compensating controls required if not compliant (critical) Must document risk and mitigation plan (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for system lifecycle. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 4.3", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 4.3 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for legacy system exemptions", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that legacy system exemptions requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "1", "clause_reference": ["1.6.1", "1.6.2", "1.6.3", "3.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "edge_case", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Cybersecurity Act 2018 §11(7)"]}}
{"test_id": "B05-014", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "Do CCoP 2.0 requirements apply to subsidiaries and affiliates of a CII operator?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Applies if subsidiary operates CII functions", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 3.2"}, {"fact": "Each entity must be registered separately", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 3.2"}, {"fact": "Group-level controls may satisfy requirements", "tier": "supporting", "source": "CCoP 2.0 3.2"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 3.2, subsidiary/affiliate scope requirements are as follows:\n\nApplies if subsidiary operates CII functions (critical) Each entity must be registered separately (important) Group-level controls may satisfy requirements (supporting).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for scope & applicability. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 3.2", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 3.2 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for subsidiary/affiliate scope", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that subsidiary/affiliate scope requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "edge_case", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B05-015", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "What controls must be in place for hardware/software supply chains?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Verify software authenticity and integrity", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 9.3.1"}, {"fact": "Source code escrow for critical vendors", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 9.3.1"}, {"fact": "Vendor security assessment required", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 9.3.1"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 3.8, supply chain control verification requirements are as follows:\n\nVerify software authenticity and integrity (critical) Source code escrow for critical vendors (important) Vendor security assessment required (critical).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for supply chain security. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 9.3.1", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 9.3.1 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for supply chain control verification", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that supply chain control verification requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.8.1", "3.8.2", "3.8.3"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "edge_case", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B05-016", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "What are the CCoP requirements for employee-owned mobile devices accessing CII systems?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "MDM/EMM solution required", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.3.4"}, {"fact": "Containerization for corporate data", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.3.4"}, {"fact": "Remote wipe capability mandatory", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.3.4"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 5.11, mobile device management requirements are as follows:\n\nMDM/EMM solution required (critical) Containerization for corporate data (critical) Remote wipe capability mandatory (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for endpoint security. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 5.3.4", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 5.3.4 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for mobile device management", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that mobile device management requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.11.1", "5.11.2", "5.11.3", "5.11.4"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "edge_case", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B05-017", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "How do CCoP 2.0 patching requirements apply to operational technology systems with limited downtime windows?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Risk-based approach acceptable", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.1.2"}, {"fact": "Compensating controls if immediate patching not possible", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.1.2"}, {"fact": "Document justification and timeline", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.1.2"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 6.1.2, ot system patching requirements are as follows:\n\nRisk-based approach acceptable (critical) Compensating controls if immediate patching not possible (critical) Document justification and timeline (important).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for ot security. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 6.1.2", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 6.1.2 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for ot system patching", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that ot system patching requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.1.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "edge_case", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B05-018", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "What are the CCoP requirements for transferring CII-related data across borders?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Must ensure adequate protection at destination", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.5.5"}, {"fact": "Contractual safeguards required", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.5.5"}, {"fact": "CSA notification may be required", "tier": "supporting", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.5.5"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 5.5.5, cross-border data transfer requirements are as follows:\n\nMust ensure adequate protection at destination (critical) Contractual safeguards required (important) CSA notification may be required (supporting).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for data protection. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 5.5.5", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 5.5.5 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for cross-border data transfer", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that cross-border data transfer requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.5.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "edge_case", "related_sections": [], 