{"test_id": "B05-019", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "Our internal network is isolated. Do we really need MFA for internal access?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Isolated networks still require MFA", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.2.3"}, {"fact": "Network isolation is a control, not a waiver", "tier": "important", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.2.3"}, {"fact": "All privileged access requires MFA regardless", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 5.2.3"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 5.3.1(c), mfa not required internally requirements are as follows:\n\nIsolated networks still require MFA (critical) Network isolation is a control, not a waiver (important) All privileged access requires MFA regardless (critical).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for identity & access management. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 5.2.3", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 5.2.3 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for mfa not required internally", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that mfa not required internally requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "5", "clause_reference": ["5.1.2", "5.3.1", "5.7.2"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "negative", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
{"test_id": "B05-020", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B05", "input": {"question": "We do annual penetration tests. Is that enough for vulnerability management?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Pen testing complements but does not replace vulnerability scanning", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.2.1"}, {"fact": "Quarterly external vulnerability scans still required", "tier": "critical", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.2.1"}, {"fact": "Continuous vulnerability assessment recommended", "tier": "supporting", "source": "CCoP 2.0 6.2.1"}], "expected_response": "According to CCoP 2.0 Section 6.2.1, annual pen test sufficient requirements are as follows:\n\nPen testing complements but does not replace vulnerability scanning (critical) Quarterly external vulnerability scans still required (critical) Continuous vulnerability assessment recommended (supporting).\n\nThe intent of this control is to ensure adequate security measures are in place for vulnerability management. Organizations must implement controls proportionate to their risk profile while ensuring the core requirements are met.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0, 6.2.1", "reasoning_chain": ["Identify CCoP 2.0 clause 6.2.1 as the authoritative source", "Extract specific control requirements for annual pen test sufficient", "Map requirements to organizational context and risk profile"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating that annual pen test sufficient requirements are optional or discretionary", "Confusing similar but distinct control requirements", "Attributing requirements to wrong CCoP clauses", "Specific control requirements from the cited clause", "Mandatory elements marked as critical in key_facts", "Reference to the applicable CCoP clause"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific thresholds or requirements not in CCoP 2.0", "Citing non-existent subsections or additional requirements"]}, "metadata": {"section": "6", "clause_reference": ["6.2.1"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "negative", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null}}
